    "body": "Check of the other posts that write a tap feed (from origin/main 3fc0e017b):\n\n- fanuc.cps, doosan-dnm.cps, mazak.cps, sinumerik.cps, tormach.cps, linuxcnc.cps (G84): `ff()` rounds the feed to a whole mm/min. Issue #3699 holds these six posts.\n- linuxcnc.cps G33.1: writes the pitch as `K` at 4 decimals. The fraction stays.\n- mach4.cps: keeps one mm decimal. 34.5 stays; 34.56 becomes 34.6. This is a smaller loss and is not in #3699.\n- fanuc-lathe.cps: writes feed per revolution at 4 decimals. The fraction stays.\n- heidenhain.cps: refuses a pitch or feed that its format cannot hold.\n- carvera, grbl, grblhal, mach3, tinyg, tormach-lathe: refuse a tap cycle by name.\n",
